# git diff --check whitespace exemptions.
#
# docs/P2B_QUALIFIED_REVIEW_OPERATIONS_FINAL_DESIGN.md and
# docs/ops/P2A_PRODUCTION_CUTOVER_RECORD.md use the standard Markdown
# hard-line-break convention (two trailing spaces at end of line) in their
# metadata header blocks -- real, intentional formatting, not accidental
# whitespace. Stripping it would merge those lines into one run-together
# paragraph when rendered.
docs/P2B_QUALIFIED_REVIEW_OPERATIONS_FINAL_DESIGN.md -whitespace
docs/ops/P2A_PRODUCTION_CUTOVER_RECORD.md -whitespace

# prisma/canonical/migrations/20260817_000001_p2c_waec_baseline_alignment is
# already applied to staging; its checksum is recorded in the staging
# _prisma_migrations ledger. Editing its bytes (even to drop a trailing
# blank line) would drift that checksum, so the file is intentionally left
# byte-for-byte unchanged and exempted here instead. See
# docs/ops/P2C_BLOCKER_CLOSURE_RECORD.md for the full reasoning.
prisma/canonical/migrations/20260817_000001_p2c_waec_baseline_alignment/migration.sql -whitespace
